{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r8","type":"objection","text":"The claim that lack of documented agreements is the root cause (r1) overlooks deeper interpersonal dynamics such as power imbalances and accumulated resentment.","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r9","type":"objection","text":"The assumption that a shared chore calendar will solve the problem (r5) neglects potential issues with access, willingness to use the tool, and the risk of the calendar becoming a source of policing and conflict.","depends":["r5"]},{"id":"r10","type":"objection","text":"Characterizing the friend's avoidance solely as discomfort or burnout (r3) may miss other motivations like conflict avoidance or unwillingness to take on responsibilities.","depends":["r3"]},{"id":"r11","type":"objection","text":"Framing the issue purely as coordination (r4) fails to address the emotional and relational tensions that appear central to the disputes.","depends":["r4"]},{"id":"r12","type":"problem","text":"How can the household address underlying relational tensions while implementing any coordination tool, ensuring both procedural clarity and emotional safety?"}],"uptake":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5","r6","r7"]}